   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator is \\( u = 2 x^{2} + 11 \\) with \\( u' = 4 x \\), and the denominator is \\( v = \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\) with \\( v' = \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} \\).",
         "rule_named": "identify the two pieces"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the quotient rule, \\( h'(x) = \\frac{u'v - uv'}{v^{2}} \\), with u'v first in the numerator.",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99080",
         "rule_named": "quotient rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( x = \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\): \\( u = \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{18} + 11 \\), \\( u' = \\frac{2 \\pi}{3} \\), \\( v = \\frac{1}{2} \\) and \\( v' = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\), so \\( h'\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = - 22 \\sqrt{3} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\pi^{2}}{9} + \\frac{4 \\pi}{3} \\).",
